[?2004l=== CORRELATION SCRIPT FIX SUMMARY ===

PROBLEM:
The correlate.py script was finding 0 lateral movement candidates (not 80% fewer, but 100% fewer)
from Suricata eve.json logs, while the same logic worked with Zeek logs.

ROOT CAUSE - TWO CRITICAL BUGS:

1. WRONG EVENT TYPE (Primary Bug):
   - Script checked for event_type == "netflow"
   - Suricata uses event_type == "flow"
   - This caused the script to skip ALL flow events

2. WRONG TIMESTAMP FORMAT:
   - Script used: "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"
   - Suricata format: "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f%z" (includes microseconds and timezone)
   - This would have caused parsing errors once bug #1 was fixed

FIXES APPLIED:
- Line 24: Changed event_type check from "netflow" to "flow"
- Line 15: Updated timestamp format to handle microseconds and timezone

RESULTS:
- Old script: 0 candidates detected
- Fixed script: 1+ candidates detected (including 10.1.5.23)
- Host 10.1.5.23 shows clear scanning behavior hitting multiple internal hosts
  on ports 445, 3389, 5985, 135, 22 within short time windows

The correlation logic itself was correct - it was just never processing any events.
